{
    "background_story": "Kahlani was a charismatic linguist who had a way with words. Growing up in a multicultural community, she was fascinated by the diversity of languages and expressions. She spent years collecting and studying idioms from around the world, often incorporating them into her daily conversations. Kahlani's friends and family would often joke that she could 'bend over backwards' to find the perfect idiom to describe any situation. Her love for idioms became contagious, and soon she was leading workshops and writing a popular blog on the subject. As her reputation grew, people began to say that Kahlani was the 'cream of the crop' when it came to idiomatic expressions. She took it as the highest compliment, knowing that her passion had brought people together and helped them 'break the ice' in their own communication.",
